  1822                          ; ***************************************************************************************
  1823                          ;
  1824                          ; Second Processor service points
  1825                          ;
  1826                          ; These are addresses to access the Second Processor.
  1827                          ;
  1828                          ; See circuit_tube.png
  1829                          ;
  1830                          ; The Tube interface gives access to a second processor and is partly implemented by the
  1831                          ; 'DNFS' ROM.
  1832                          ;
  1833                          ; Initialising the DNFS ROM copies 1K of Tube Operating System service code into
  1834                          ; the current language workspace at $0400-$07FF. A call to .tubeCopyLanguageROMToSecondProcessor
  1835                          ; ($0400) calls into this Tube service code. It finds and copies code from an appropriate
  1836                          ; language ROM into the second processor and runs it there. The 6502 Second Processor shipped
  1837                          ; with HI-BASIC, a version of the BASIC ROM designed to run on the second processor at a high
  1838                          ; memory address range leaving more memory (44K) for BASIC programs on the second
  1839                          ; processor.
  1840                          ;
  1841                          ; The regular standard 6502 processor is sometimes called the 'first', 'host' or I/O processor,
  1842                          ; as it has control over input and output devices like the keyboard and the display. The second
  1843                          ; processor is sometimes known as the 'parasite'.
  1844                          ;
  1845                          ; See NAUG Section 18.4, Page 330
  1846                          ;
  1847                          ; ***************************************************************************************
  1848                          .tubeCopyLanguageROMToSecondProcessor       = $0400     ; copy a language ROM code to the
  1849                                                                                  ; second processor
  1850                          .tubeCopyESCAPEFlagToSecondProcessor        = $0403     ;
  1851                          .tubeTransferData                           = $0406     ;
  1852                          
