 20004                          ; This area of memory from $FC00-$FF00 is the memory mapped IO space, so this memory cannot
 20005                          ; be used as a normal part of the OS. Instead the memory locations store a string of credits.
 20006                          ; For memory mapped I/O, see Chapter 3.
